  "validation": "BREP/IO debug and release each pass 496 all-feature tests; minimal release passes 488, with no ignored cases. Both warning-denied all-target Clippy configurations, rustdoc, six examples, eleven optional OCCT reader checks, fuzz-target compilation and 71 zero-import source-path WASM groups pass. The earlier focused conic/oblique and STEP circle/pcurve regressions pass 3 and 13 tests. Independent exact expectations and the original full-size fixtures are unchanged. All fifteen preceding continuation diagnostics succeed; the nine-fixture frontier records 56 native results, 7 undecided, 6 unsupported and 12 unavailable dependent steps, separately from semantic admission. All 22 previous STEP artifacts remain byte-identical. Both targeted scalar zero-factor reproductions still fail with FACTORS > 0; they remain failed gates, not pre-push exemptions.",
  "cost_evidence": "The full 90-process campaign preserves all receipts across 159 cases and fifteen corpora. Maximum case-median candidate/baseline latency is 1.035024; 0 rows exceed 10%, and 33 rows change allocation observations, including 2 with increased calls or requested bytes. All raw samples, allocation requests, process resources, executable sizes and adverse rows are retained. The six-case focused probe is preserved separately. Shared-host observations do not establish a controlled-host speedup, total-resource bound or closure of prior cost gates. Native harness size changes range from 0 to 1208 bytes; the WASM probe grows 275 bytes. These are harness sizes, not shipped-package measurements.",
  "limits": "Only the BREP periodic conic helper changes in production. No persistent cache, dependency implementation, public API, archive schema, predicate policy or input domain changes. All 28 work packages remain open. General oblique closure, curved-shell embedding, cone/torus STEP, operation-wide provenance/certainty and internal work/heap/cancellation contracts remain open. The stronger diagonal-cone diagnostics inherited from upstream are not promoted to semantic admission here. WASM uses workspace paths. Package/MSRV, actual C/Python/JS consumers, coverage, machine-checked proofs, runtime fuzz/ASan, lexicase and full-workspace/pre-push gates remain open. No push was performed.",
  "decision": "kept",
  "retention_rationale": "Retained after the complete preserved correctness and cost campaign. The helper reuses strict decided orderings for the same immutable value/domain and changes no accepted geometry, endpoint identity or deterministic output contract. Both partial pcurve cases remove 656 allocation calls and 45,904 requested bytes per operation; their observed full-campaign time ratios are 0.971130 and 0.977347. All 159 cases preserve their receipts and no case-median time ratio exceeds 1.035024. The two similarity matrices with increased allocation observations remain visible; each increase is less than 0.075% of its corresponding baseline. Native harness growth of up to 1,208 bytes and WASM growth of 275 bytes are retained as adverse size observations. These shared-host samples justify this limited local reuse; they do not establish a general speedup, universal allocation reduction or closure of earlier performance, resource, correctness or release gates.",
